==English==

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{m|en|exponent}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v}}</ref> Perhaps from {{m|en|exponentiation}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɛkspəˈnɛnʃi.eɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-exponentiate.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|mathematics}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To use [[exponentiation]].
##: {{ux|en|In order to solve the equation we must '''exponentiate'''.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[raise]] (a [[number]] or [[mathematical]] [[expression]]) to a [[power]];  to [[apply]] an [[exponent]] to a mathematical expression.
##: {{ux|en|Let us '''exponentiate''' ''x'' to obtain ''x<sup>n</sup>''.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} To [[apply]] a [[mathematical]] [[exponentiation]] [[function]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[increase]] (something) [[exponentially]].

